------------------------------------------------------------------------

F4 — the declaration is presentable before installation

  ok    names the one host it may contact
  ok    names the one entity it may read
  ok    says it cannot control anything
  ok    says it cannot see other integrations' passwords
  ok    says who declared it
  ok    shows the resource limits
  ok    shows no content hash
  ok    lists more denials than grants
  ok    an undeclared integration renders as no permissions at all
  ok    an unreadable declaration says so, and says why
  ok    a changed integration says the code changed
  ok    ...and says the permissions did not
  ok    a derived manifest says it was not the author's
  ok    ...and asks the user to check it

PASS — every state an integration can be in has a rendering, the denials are
       shown at the same weight as the grants, and no digest is presented.
